This test exercises the "Nash Zero Pressure Kernel" 
There is a 'functorized version' of the kernel in GPU_Collide_Stream_Iolets.hpp
as well as just a regular __global__ function. 

in main.cu the test function runs both and compares the results against the 
"expectation" which comes from exercising the kernel (__global__ function version)
in the real application. Appropriate inputs and expected outputs are dumped into 
the 'nash_data_1.h' file. Float arrays are dumped as byte arrays to keep bit identicality
with the original scenario.

The file contents are as follows:

api.h :   Kernel launchig + macros (mini portable API implemented in HIP)

GPU_Collide_Stream_Iolets.hpp: 
	This contains the kernels both the functor form and the '__global__' function form
	The file also contains a device function the kernels call.
	Finally the '__global__ function' version relies on some constant memory so this file
	contains a setup() function to fill the constant memory symbols from the 'nash_data_1.h' file

nash_data_1.h: the input data to the kernels and expected output data.

main.cu: the test code.


NB: There is overall only 1 compilation unit. main.cu includes GPU_Collide_Stream_Iolets.hpp, which
in turn incldes the api.h and nash_data_1.h file.

To run, just run:  

make


